<title>EGYPT: Egypt says buys 250,000T Argentine wheat.</title>
<headline>Egypt says buys 250,000T Argentine wheat.</headline>
<dateline>CAIRO 1996-11-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Egyptian state's General Authority for Supply Commodities (GASC) said on Saturday it was buying 250,000 tonnes of Argentine wheat. GASC vice chairman Samir Shakankiri told Reuters the breakdown was:</p>
<p>- 50,000 tonnes at $134.5 FOB from Cargill for loading December 12 to 31.</p>
<p>- 50,000 tonnes at $132.5 from Romak for January loading.</p>
<p>- 100,000 tonnes at $132.5 from Toepfer for January loading.</p>
<p>- 50,000 tonnes at $132.85 from Molinos for January 15 to 31 loading.</p>
<p>-- Christine Hauser +20 2 578 3290/1</p>
